upplied. No full-text review or novelty certification claimed.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"ref.Tibshirani2019\",\n      \"paper_id\": \"arxiv:1904.06019\",\n      \"citation_key\": \"Tibshirani2019\",\n      \"title\": \"Conformal Prediction Under Covariate Shift\",\n      \"year\": 2019,\n      \"query\": \"Direct identifier lookup: arxiv:1904.06019\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://arxiv.org/abs/1904.06019\",\n      \"retrieved_at\": \"2026-11-07T06:32:13.622671+00:00\",\n      \"reading_path\": \"literature/Tibshirani2019/reading.json\",\n      \"reading_scope\": \"Read the official abstract and downloaded full text where available; citation claims restricted to described method and guarantee scope.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"ref.Angelopoulos2021\",\n      \"paper_id\": \"arxiv:2107.07511\",\n      \"citation_key\": \"Angelopoulos2021\",\n      \"title\": \"A Gentle Introduction to Conformal Prediction and Distribution-Free Uncertainty Quantification\",\n      \"year\": 2021,\n      \"query\": \"Direct identifier lookup: arxiv:2107.07511\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://arxiv.org/abs/2107.07511\",\n      \"retrieved_at\": \"2026-11-07T06:32:13.622671+00:00\",\n{\n  \"claims\": [\n    {\n      \"claim\": \"Homosk. held-out condition means in the abstract, main text, Table 1 and Figure 2: euclidean: coverage=0.900052083, volume=0.178176117; ilr: coverage=0.899114583, volume=0.128428650; adaptive: coverage=0.898333333, volume=0.128591156\",\n      \"source_ids\": [\n        \"final.evidence.episodes\"\n      ],\n      \"citation_keys\": []\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim\": \"Heterosk. held-out condition means in the abstract, main text, Table 1 and Figure 2: euclidean: coverage=0.903020833, volume=0.333621216; ilr: coverage=0.903437500, volume=0.335896301; adaptive: coverage=0.904375000, volume=0.147566223\",\n      \"source_ids\": [\n        \"final.evidence.episodes\"\n      ],\n      \"citation_keys\": []\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim\": \"Boundary held-out condition means in the abstract, main text, Table 1 and Figure 2: euclidean: coverage=0.899166667, volume=0.715514374; ilr: coverage=0.901614583, volume=0.999997711; adaptive: coverage=0.894739583, volume=0.975856018\",\n      \"source_ids\": [\n        \"final.evidence.episodes\"\n      ],\n      \"citation_keys\": []\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim\": \"Shifted held-out condition means in the abstract, main text, Table 1 and Figure 2: euclidean: coverage=0.859218750, volume=0.192813110; ilr: coverage=0.708177083, volume=0.614458466; adaptive: coverage=0.863281250, volume=0.622106934\",\n      \"source_ids\": [\n        \"final.evidence.episodes\"\n      ],\n      \"citation_keys\": []\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim\": \"Constant held-out condition means in the abstract, main text, Table 1 and Figure 2: euclidean: coverage=0.905416667, volume=0.816603851; ilr: coverage=0.901770833, volume=0.740297699; adaptive: coverage=0.901927083, volume=0.693161011\",\n      \"source_ids\": [\n        \"final.evidence.episodes\"\n      ],\n      \"citation_keys\": []\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim\": \"Unpaired held-out condition means in the abstract, main text, Table 1 and Figure 2: euclidean: coverage=0.906718750, volume=0.823188782; ilr: coverage=0.900520833, volume=0.746241760; adaptive: coverage=0.902291667, volume=0.700424194\",\n      \"source_ids\": [\n        \"final.evidence.episodes\"\n      ],\n      \"citation_keys\": []\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim\": \"Adaptive volume is smaller than both references in every held-out heteroskedastic seed; this is an empirical configuration comparison, not population or component superiority.\",\n      \"source_ids\": [\n        \"final.evidence.episodes\"\n      ],\n      \"citation_keys\": []\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim\": \"Abstract and all held-out plots use five seeds, six conditions, three methods, nominal coverage 0.90, and all retained seed observations; Figure 3 shows four overlapping descriptive sign strata in