ator-owned ridge locations in ILR coordinates with an unscaled residual norm; isolates a meaningful coordinate-space reference using the same external calibration and simplex-volume measure, without claiming a matched-training-size mechanism ablation.\"}, {\"name\": \"Four-fold residual adaptive ILR ellipsoids\", \"role\": \"proposed\", \"include_reason\": \"Frozen selected model and sole adaptive method with released final evidence; describe as the studied configuration rather than an established novel algorithm or universal winner.\"}, {\"name\": \"Single-split residual adaptive ILR ellipsoids\", \"role\": \"ablation\", \"include_reason\": \"Three search-seed measurements support a limited direct comparison with the four-fold configuration; the change bundles residual fitting, full-data location refitting, and training-data allocation, so it cannot identify a pure cross-fitting effect.\"}, {\"name\": \"Continuously interpolated covariance ellipsoids\", \"role\": \"ablation\", \"include_reason\": \"Three search-seed measurements test continuous covariance interpolation against hard routing while retaining four-fold residual fitting; show no established advantage and keep this auxiliary branch out of the central thesis.\"}]\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
