ent(\n246:    parser.add_argument(\n251:    parser.add_argument(\n256:    parser.add_argument(\n261:    parser.add_argument(\n267:    parser.add_argument(\n273:    parser.add_argument(\n278:    parser.add_argument(\n390:            \"append_memory: --global-memory-md and --global-memory-jsonl are required \"\nUse the documented candidate RPC to constrain experiment design: training-fitted ILR locations and Cholesky shapes are controllable, whereas alternative conformal score families, separate group quantiles, structural-zero experiments, and evaluator-side uncertainty instrumentation are not. Investigate training-only residual estimation changes, such as out-of-fold residuals with all-row location refitting, as hypotheses rather than established improvements. Preserve external calibration and fixed row-wise prediction; shape adaptation alone does not establish group-conditional coverage. A correct aggregate evaluation with an overall rubric failure does not identify a protocol defect or a scientific mechanism failure; seek explicit criterion evidence before prescribing repairs. Do not turn a single aggregate selection score into a replicated superiority claim or fabricate uncertainty unavailable from released measurements.\n8e787600f898cef72481b1f905fc41d43445f9b8b3edc1efe2923f9328e0085c  paper.tex\n39fc322b5863088b3bcd1b1bf89324d574b30965112761d7862ba38b56374c66  references.bib\nbe4bc9fd69e56f9ec7bc6fb61c75af5e6624746a652c1003cd0d5630e11a6748  references_provenance.json\nReference titles:\nVovk2005: Algorithmic Learning in a Random World\nPapadopoulos2002: Inductive Confidence Machines for Regression\nLei2018: Distribution-Free Predictive Inference for Regression\nBarber2021Jackknife: Predictive inference with the jackknife+\nTibshirani2019: Conformal Prediction Under Covariate Shift\nAngelopoulos2021: A Gentle Introduction to Conformal Prediction and Distribution-Free Uncertainty Quantification\nAitchison1982: The Statistical Analysis of Compositional Data\nEgozc